# examples/regressions/user_prog_arena_alloc — the §16 runtime-prelude INJECTION fixture
# (`docs/design/plano-s16-runtime-prelude-injection.md` crumb I0, fixture RF1). An ORDINARY
# project: its own `src` source root, NO `teko::runtime`/`arena.tks` and NO `teko::sys` of its
# own. It allocates a `[]i64` of 10000, sums it, and concatenates strings — a normal program that
# exercises the arena through `teko::list::push`. Crumb I0 injects the compiler-shipped Teko arena
# (`src/runtime/arena.tks`) + `teko::sys` into this program's file set, so its emitted `teko.c`
# now DEFINES `teko_teko__runtime__region_alloc` (previously undefined for an ordinary program)
# while still allocating on the C arena (the injected arena is emitted-but-dormant until crumb E
# flips `cg_arena_sym`). The harness observes exit 0: injection is behavior-transparent.
name = "user_prog_arena_alloc"
source = "src"

[artifact]
kind = "binary"
